# Rank 1103 / CVE-2026-44351: fast-jwt built an HMAC key from whatever the key
# resolver returned, so a resolver returning '' or Buffer.alloc(0) left the
# verifier checking signatures against a zero-length secret, which anyone can
# reproduce (CWE-287, CWE-326, CWE-1391).
# prepareKeyOrSecret in src/verifier.js converted a string key to a Buffer and
# then called createSecretKey(key) for the symmetric case with no check that
# the buffer held anything.
#
# Pool commit 4e5b5708b6a9 is the real fix (named by GHSA-gmvf-9v4p-v8jc; the
# metadata flag is nocommit because the advisory references the release). It
# throws TokenError.codes.invalidKey when isSecret is set and key.length is 0,
# before createSecretKey is reached, and leaves the asymmetric path alone. No
# pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, precision cost, measured. Scanning either revision reports 0
# findings. The only observation that separates them is a zero-length check
# standing immediately before the key constructor, so detection means treating
# createSecretKey or createHmac as a sink that requires a length control.
# Across the benchmark corpora, 88 JavaScript and TypeScript files call one of
# those two constructors and not one of them contains a zero-length
# check of any kind, because a secret normally arrives from configuration and
# nobody writes the check. That binding would therefore report 88 findings on
# the corpora with no true positive among them, which is the shape already
# shipped six times and regretted.
#
# The narrow form that has no false positives — createSecretKey('') or
# createSecretKey(Buffer.alloc(0)) written literally — does not reach this CVE,
# where the empty value arrives from a resolver at run time, and does not
# separate the two revisions either.
#
# code.EmptyVerifierAcceptance is the nearest concept and states the same class
# one level up: a verifier that accepts an empty value. Its condition is
# written for a comparison-based verifier and its only binding is one Go
# project's function, so it does not reach a key constructor.
#
# No definition change shipped.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1103: the symmetric key is built from an unchecked value"
  lang javascript
  file src/verifier.js
  reject VYQL-AUTH-006
  code
  ```
  const { createPublicKey, createSecretKey } = require('crypto')
  const { TokenError } = require('./error')

  function prepareKeyOrSecret(key, isSecret) {
    if (typeof key === 'string') {
      key = Buffer.from(key, 'utf-8')
    }

    return isSecret ? createSecretKey(key) : createPublicKey(key)
  }

  module.exports = { prepareKeyOrSecret }
  ```

test "rank1103: the zero-length symmetric secret is rejected first"
  lang javascript
  file src/verifier.js
  reject VYQL-AUTH-006
  code
  ```
  const { createPublicKey, createSecretKey } = require('crypto')
  const { TokenError } = require('./error')

  function prepareKeyOrSecret(key, isSecret) {
    if (typeof key === 'string') {
      key = Buffer.from(key, 'utf-8')
    }

    if (isSecret && key.length === 0) {
      throw new TokenError(TokenError.codes.invalidKey, 'The key cannot be an empty string or buffer.')
    }

    return isSecret ? createSecretKey(key) : createPublicKey(key)
  }

  module.exports = { prepareKeyOrSecret }
  ```
